  "Number": 7,
  "Question": "Mary is \\(20\\%\\) older than Sally, and Sally is \\(40\\%\\) younger than Danielle. The sum of their ages is \\(23.2\\) years. How old will Mary be on her next birthday?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(7\\)",
    "B": "\\(8\\)",
    "C": "\\(9\\)",
    "D": "\\(10\\)",
    "E": "\\(11\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The two percentages refer to different people, so first express every age as a percentage of Danielle's age.\n\nSally is \\(100\\%-40\\%=60\\%\\) of Danielle's age. Mary is \\(100\\%+20\\%=120\\%\\) of Sally's age, so Mary is \\(1.2\\cdot60\\%=72\\%\\) of Danielle's age.\n\nTheir combined age is therefore \\(100\\%+60\\%+72\\%=232\\%\\) of Danielle's age. Thus Danielle's age is\n\\[\n23.2\\div2.32=10\\text{ years}.\n\\]\nMary is currently \\(0.72\\cdot10=7.2\\) years old. She is between her seventh and eighth birthdays, so she will be \\(\\boxed{8}\\) on her next birthday, choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
